WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.428
"Are you sure the threatening comment is gone?" Maggie asked.

2
00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:21.058
"It's no big deal, kids." Jackson sounded distracted.

3
00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:25.278
"Maybe the mayor deleted it." He pulled out his notebook.

4
00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:30.779
"I think I'll talk to the police and see if they found anything suspicious in Mrs. Sweet's shed.

5
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.708
You kids should go home and work on your float."

6
00:00:33.709 --> 00:00:37.767
"Are you sure you don't want any help?" Henry asked.

7
00:00:37.768 --> 00:00:41.656
"The Lemonade Detectives have solved lots of mysteries."

8
00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:45.596
Jackson smiled. "I know, Henry. But don't worry.

9
00:00:45.597 --> 00:00:51.880
If there's really a mystery here, I'll get to the bottom of it."

10
00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:56.819
He rushed off, whistling cheerfully. Henry glanced at Maggie.

11
00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.950
"Should we follow him and try to talk him into letting us hear what the police say?"

12
00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:05.553
"No, Jackson is right," Maggie said.

13
00:01:05.554 --> 00:01:09.447
"We need to finish our float, or we'll never win those prizes."

14
00:01:09.448 --> 00:01:12.485
"I guess you're right." Henry smiled.

15
00:01:12.486 --> 00:01:17.991
"Maybe I just miss solving mysteries so much that I was hoping we'd found another one!"

16
00:01:17.992 --> 00:01:23.547
Maggie shrugged. "Not me. Nobody is offering to pay our detective fee.

17
00:01:23.548 --> 00:01:26.673
That means we don't have time to investigate."

18
00:01:26.674 --> 00:01:29.514
The two of them headed out of the auto shop.

19
00:01:29.515 --> 00:01:34.767
Right outside Henry spotted Snake leaning against a lamppost.

20
00:01:34.768 --> 00:01:36.975
"Hi, Snake," Henry said.

21
00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:40.606
"Is your band's float ready for the parade tomorrow?"

22
00:01:40.607 --> 00:01:46.377
"Hi, Lemonade Kids." Snake sighed. "We're not doing a float after all."

23
00:01:46.378 --> 00:01:50.075
"Really? What happened?" Maggie asked.

24
00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:53.821
"Our practice was going great yesterday," Snake said.

25
00:01:53.822 --> 00:01:57.634
"We were all having so much fun that we forgot about the time.

26
00:01:57.635 --> 00:02:01.238
One member of the band got grounded for coming home late."

27
00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:04.867
"Wow, that's too bad," Henry said.

28
00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:08.535
"So the whole band is dropping out of the parade?"

29
00:02:08.536 --> 00:02:11.836
"We don't have much choice." Snake shrugged.

30
00:02:11.837 --> 00:02:15.380
"Our music wouldn't sound right without all of us playing."

31
00:02:15.381 --> 00:02:23.136
"Oh. Well . . . sorry," Henry said. "See you around."

32
00:02:23.137 --> 00:02:25.376
He and Maggie wandered off.

33
00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:29.223
Maggie glanced back to make sure Snake was out of earshot.

34
00:02:29.224 --> 00:02:34.502
"Snake looked pretty upset," she said. "But this is good news for us.

35
00:02:34.503 --> 00:02:38.373
It means we'll have less competition for those prizes!"

36
00:02:38.374 --> 00:02:41.771
Henry nodded, but he wasn't really listening.

37
00:02:41.772 --> 00:02:45.086
He'd just noticed the town hall building up ahead.

38
00:02:45.087 --> 00:02:51.714
"Jackson said Mayor Porter might have deleted that threatening comment from the website," he said.

39
00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:55.646
"Maybe we should stop in and ask the mayor if that's true."

40
00:02:55.647 --> 00:03:00.518
Maggie looked uncertain. "Do you still think there's a mystery going on?"

41
00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:03.084
"I don't know," Henry said.

42
00:03:03.085 --> 00:03:10.055
"It's possible that the threatening comment was a joke, and Mrs. Sweet just misplaced her candy.

43
00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:15.357
But it's also possible that someone is trying to ruin the parade."

44
00:03:15.358 --> 00:03:23.280
"Okay," Maggie said. "But let's hurry. I want to get back to our float soon."

45
00:03:23.281 --> 00:03:28.011
They went into the town hall building.

46
00:03:28.012 --> 00:03:32.218
The mayor's secretary was a cheerful young man named Mr. Beck.

47
00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:37.651
"I'm sorry, kids," he said after Henry and Maggie asked to see the mayor.

48
00:03:37.652 --> 00:03:40.867
"Mayor Porter has meetings all afternoon.

49
00:03:40.868 --> 00:03:44.177
I can make an appointment for you on Monday, if you like."

50
00:03:44.178 --> 00:03:49.269
"Monday's too late," Maggie said. "It's about the parade tomorrow."

51
00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:52.611
Henry nodded. "It might be important."

52
00:03:52.612 --> 00:03:56.724
"Might be?" Mr. Beck echoed. "What do you mean?"

53
00:03:56.725 --> 00:04:02.332
"We're afraid someone might be trying to sabotage the parade," Henry said.

54
00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:06.420
"Mrs. Sweet thinks someone broke into her shed last night.

55
00:04:06.421 --> 00:04:11.089
And there was a threatening message in the comments on the town website."

56
00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:16.955
"Oh dear. Really?" Mr. Beck quickly opened the town website on his computer.

57
00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:21.346
"I didn't notice anything like that when I was updating the site a few minutes ago."

58
00:04:21.347 --> 00:04:25.360
"You mean you didn't delete the comment?" Maggie asked.

59
00:04:25.361 --> 00:04:27.865
"Only the person who leaves the comment can delete it."

60
00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:32.032
Mr. Beck sounded skeptical now. "What did you kids see?"

61
00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:37.402
"There was a message right after the one by Miss Bishop," Henry explained.

62
00:04:37.403 --> 00:04:43.446
"It said the parade was for losers, and the mayor should cancel it, or else."

63
00:04:43.447 --> 00:04:48.834
"Hmm." A second later Mr. Beck closed the town website page.

64
00:04:48.835 --> 00:04:52.021
"Well, I'll mention the comment to the mayor when I see him."

65
00:04:52.022 --> 00:04:56.272
Henry could tell the secretary wasn't taking this seriously.

66
00:04:56.273 --> 00:04:58.504
"But what if—," he began.

67
00:04:58.505 --> 00:05:02.502
"This is an outrage!" an angry shout interrupted him.

68
00:05:02.503 --> 00:05:06.878
An older, white-haired man had just stomped into the office.

69
00:05:06.879 --> 00:05:10.311
He looked familiar, but Henry didn't know his name.

70
00:05:10.312 --> 00:05:13.899
"Good afternoon, Mr. Fleming," Mr. Beck greeted the older man.

71
00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.587
"Is something wrong?"

72
00:05:15.588 --> 00:05:18.621
"You bet your life something's wrong!"

73
00:05:18.622 --> 00:05:23.384
Mr. Fleming pushed past Henry and Maggie and glared at the secretary.

74
00:05:23.385 --> 00:05:27.185
"The window of my art studio overlooks an empty lot.

75
00:05:27.186 --> 00:05:30.078
I like it that way—very quiet.

76
00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:34.282
But this week the high school soccer team has been building a float there.

77
00:05:34.283 --> 00:05:39.497
So there's been hammering, sawing, shouting, and laughing all day long.

78
00:05:39.498 --> 00:05:41.665
I can't take it anymore!

79
00:05:41.666 --> 00:05:49.160
If someone doesn't do something, I'll sue the town to call off the parade!"
